From 522c7ed280d715761c14a3b26ea8b6fdd4316cd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 19:25:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 147/638] ui: add native AROS Ozone backend [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-ozone

AI_STATUS: implemented

ROOT_CAUSE: The AROS port could render through Chromium's headless platform but had no PlatformWindow, screen, or SurfaceOzoneCanvas implementation capable of opening an Intuition window and presenting compositor pixels.

FIX_REASON: Add an in-tree AROS Ozone backend with native Intuition window ownership, a shared IDCMP port, public-screen discovery, a Skia BGRA raster canvas, and cybergraphics damage presentation. Keep unsupported GPU and native-pixmap capabilities explicit so graphics.hidd/Gallium/Vulkan acceleration can be added behind the same platform boundary.

SCOPE: New ui/ozone/platform/aros source set only; no platform is selected until the separate registration commit.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-windowed -j1 ui/ozone:ozone completed successfully after compiling every new backend source.

RISK: medium; the first slice is software-presented and polls IDCMP at 8 ms pending direct MessagePumpAROS signal integration, while shared-port teardown follows Intuition's explicit ownership contract.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
